mation, indicating a technical subsection that operationalizes the right within the LGPD. The connection TI_SEC_001 -> ARTIGO 9º highlights how this technical artifact supports information access rights and their implementation [Data: Entities (380); Relationships (376)].\"},{\"summary\":\"Inter-article connectivity and regulatory modularity\",\"explanation\":\"ARTIGO 9º and ARTIGO 18 are elements of the same regulatory framework (LGPD) and are described as related but distinct rights, reflecting a modular structure where information access sustains multiple data subject rights. The relationships ARTIGO 9º ↔ ARTIGO 18 and LGPD ↔ ARTIGO 18 illustrate a network designed to empower individuals with control over personal data [Data: Entities (378, 379); Relationships (375, 374)].\"},{\"summary\":\"Regulatory governance implications and compliance signal\",\"explanation\":\"The documented network indicates that compliance programs should address both the rights to information and broader data subject rights under LGPD. The presence of TI_SEC_001 as a dedicated technical artifact supporting the right to information signals a structured approach for implementing these rights within organizational processes and governance frameworks [Data: Entities (380, 378); Relationships (376, 374)].\"}],\"rating\":4.0,\"rating_explanation\":\"Moderate regulatory impact due to explicit rights and information access requirements within LGPD and their interdependencies.\"}"}, "metrics": {"attempted_request_count": 1, "successful_response_count": 0, "failed_response_count": 0, "responses_with_tokens": 1, "prompt_tokens": 2503, "completion_tokens": 5111, "total_tokens": 7614, "compute_duration_seconds": 28.109153985977173, "streaming_responses": 0, "retries": 0, "requests_with_retries": 0}}}